# Progress UI design

Visual north star: [Linear DESIGN.md](https://github.com/VoltAgent/awesome-design-md/tree/main/design-md/linear.app) (dense, precise, calm tool UI). Adapt to this app — do not clone Linear’s lavender marketing brand.

## Stack constraints

- Tokens live in `src/app/globals.css` (shadcn / oklch). Prefer `bg-background`, `bg-muted`, `bg-card`, `border`, `text-muted-foreground`, `ring` over hard-coded hex.
- Fonts: Geist Sans / Geist Mono already wired — keep them; no new display families for product chrome.
- Light + dark both ship; every surface must work in both themes.
- Product chrome is a working board (sidebar + roadmap + chat), not a marketing landing page.

## Atmosphere

- Quiet software craft: high information density, low decoration.
- Hierarchy via surface lift + hairline borders, not shadows / glow / gradients.
- Accent color is scarce: primary actions, focus rings, active nav — never large fills or section backgrounds.
- “无压” means calm copy and uncluttered lanes, not empty marketing whitespace.

## Layout & density

- Spacing scale preference: 4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 24 / 32. Prefer tight gaps in lists and boards.
- Sidebar + main content: one clear composition; avoid dashboard-of-cards chrome.
- Cards only when they wrap a real interaction (task, dialog, approval). If border/bg/radius can go without hurting clarity, drop them.
- Prefer rows / lanes / compact lists over padded feature tiles.
- Radius: stick to existing `--radius` (≈ shadcn md). Primary buttons ≈ 8px feel; reserve pills for tiny status chips only — not CTAs.

## Components

- Buttons: primary for the one decisive action; ghost/secondary for the rest. Compact padding (≈ `8px 14px` feel via existing Button sizes).
- Inputs: muted surface, hairline border, clear focus ring (`ring`), no heavy inset shadows.
- Dialogs / sheets: one job, short header, no decorative hero art.
- Chat: readable body type, restrained bubbles; tool-approval cards stay scannable (before/after), not flashy.
- Status / badges: small, muted; project color dots may stay chromatic (domain data), but don’t add a second global brand accent.

## Do

- Reuse `components/ui/*` before inventing new primitives.
- Keep type mostly regular/medium; headings semibold, not ultra-bold display.
- Collapse chrome on mobile (drawer nav already); keep ≥40px tap targets on controls.
- Match surrounding patterns in `sidebar`, `roadmap-board`, agent panels.

## Don’t

- Don’t add purple-on-white / indigo glow themes, cream+terracotta “AI default” looks, or broadsheet newspaper layouts.
- Don’t use atmospheric gradients, spotlight cards, emoji clusters, or multi-layer shadows.
- Don’t pill-round primary CTAs or flood the UI with accent fills.
- Don’t build marketing sections (stats strips, logo clouds, hero slogans) inside the app shell.
- Don’t introduce a second chromatic accent system beyond existing semantic tokens + per-project colors.
